---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — KitnaSIP" description="Who is behind KitnaSIP, and why it exists." path="/about">
  <section class="prose">
    <h1>About KitnaSIP</h1>

    <div class="post-meta">
      <span class="byline author-lg">
        <img src={AUTHOR.photo} alt={AUTHOR.name} width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
        <span class="who">{AUTHOR.name}</span>
      </span>
    </div>

    <p>
      KitnaSIP started from a simple frustration: every SIP calculator tells you the amount
      you <em>need</em>, but none checks the amount you can actually <em>afford</em>. If you're a salaried
      professional in India trying to plan honestly, that gap is exactly where the anxiety lives.
    </p>

    <h2>What this tool does — and doesn't</h2>
    <p>
      KitnaSIP takes your income, expenses, goal and horizon, adjusts the goal for inflation, and
      shows you the monthly SIP it really needs — then compares that to your surplus and gives you
      levers to close any gap. It's free, needs no signup, and there's nothing to buy.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is an <strong>educational tool, not investment advice</strong>. KitnaSIP never recommends
      specific mutual funds. It shows illustrative projections based on assumptions you control, and
      points you to fund <em>categories</em> to research — never named funds to buy. For a personal
      plan, please consult a SEBI-registered investment adviser.
    </p>

    <h2>How KitnaSIP is funded</h2>
    <p>
      KitnaSIP is free to use. If it ever earns anything, it's through a fixed referral fee when
      someone chooses to open a demat account via a partner link, and through display advertising —
      never by charging for advice or selling fund recommendations. Those payouts never change what
      you pay or what the tool shows you.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes this</h2>
    <p>
      {AUTHOR.name} — {AUTHOR.bio} Have a question or spotted something wrong? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
